hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1449","On the authority of Ali bin Hajr Al-Saadi, on the authority of Ismail bin Jaafar, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Iyadh bin Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out on the day of Al-Adha and Al-Fitr, and he would begin to pray. His prayer and peace, he stood up and faced the people while they were sitting in their place of prayer. If he had a need to be sent or otherwise, he mentioned it. for the people, and if he had a need he would command them to fulfill it, and he would say: “Give in charity. Give in charity. Give in charity.” And he was the one who gave alms most of the time to women, then He left, and it remained like that until Marwan bin Al-Hakam arrived. I went out and confronted Marwan until we came to the prayer place, and behold, Kathir bin Al-Salt had built it. A pulpit made of clay and brick, and when Marwan was wresting his hand with me as if he was dragging me towards the pulpit, and I was dragging him towards the prayer place, so when I saw that From him, I said: Where do we begin to pray? Marwan said: O Abu Saeed, abandon what you know, so I raised my voice: No, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, do not bring anything better than what I know, three times, then I left"
